WEBVTT

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:21.530
The Alchemist's power has stopped
the destruction of the books.

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:25.650
But there's no way to stop
the tainting of Akutagawa's novels.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:26.940
At this rate...

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:48.190
Where are you going?

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:53.030
Where else? I'm going to delve.

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:55.980
I'm going to purify Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> 's books.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:01.690
Not just <i>Gears</i> . I have to save them all.

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:02.860
Impossible.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:05.480
What about the others?

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:07.480
If we work together...

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:08.900
They're gone.

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:12.110
You're the only author left.

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:19.610
The souls of the authors were shattered
and sealed within their books.

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:23.190
They can't go back to what they were.

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:24.400
Damn!

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.440
Then I'll go alone!

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:30.690
It's reckless!

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:34.110
You can't beat that Taint alone!

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.320
I have to go anyway!

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.610
What did you say?

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:43.940
What is it?

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:47.150
If we can free the sealed souls,

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:51.940
we may be able to bring back the authors, he says.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:53.480
Is that true?

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.940
No, it's impossible.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:57.900
With their souls shattered,

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:02.480
we'd need a power equal to reincarnation
to summon them once more.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:05.530
Even the Alchemist couldn't...

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:10.980
No! You mustn't!

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.730
What's it saying?

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:16.320
The possibility that it works is incredibly slim.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:22.440
But using all its power, it may be able
to rewrite the laws of the library, or...

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:30.070
But it will destroy this body, it says.

00:04:30.070 --> 00:04:34.610
This stone exists to express the power
and will of the Alchemist.

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:39.730
If it were to shatter, the Library
would lose the Alchemist's protection.

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:42.780
I'll do it.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:44.030
What?

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:48.860
If I purify <i>Gears</i> , I can release
everyone who's inside, right?

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:50.030
Then I'll do it!

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:52.230
Were you listening?

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:56.780
How do we fight the Taints without
the power of the Alchemist from now on?

00:04:56.780 --> 00:05:00.190
If we don't do something now,
there will be no "from now on!"

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:13.400
You're right.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:15.940
Dazai.

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:18.280
I'm counting on you.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:58.440
Why can't I cut it?

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:00.900
Of course you can't.

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:05.070
The person in the raincoat has no physical form.

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:09.570
One of Ryunosuke Akutagawa's
most famous late works, <i>Gears</i> .

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:14.150
The person in the raincoat that continually
appears before the protagonist,

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:16.280
and the turning of the gears,

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:20.980
have both been interpreted as an expression
of the author's indescribable fear.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:23.650
This novel has no clear plot.

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:26.150
It represents the author's fear

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:31.070
and the death that approaches them.

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:34.320
The protagonist is likely representative
of the author himself.

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:37.400
These fears drive him near to madness,

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:42.480
and the story ends when his beloved
wife tells him that he's about to die.

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:46.110
What's wrong?

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:49.400
Nothing.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:53.190
Nothing's wrong, but...

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:58.690
But somehow, it felt as if
you were going to die.

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:03.690
This story is a story of pure despair.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:06.690
If you read it, you doubtless agree, right?

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:08.030
You...!

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:14.150
You won't call me "Akutagawa" anymore, will you?

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:18.320
I've seen him more,
been closer to him, than anyone.

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:21.150
I've seen his fear.

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:25.230
Each time he wrote,
he sacrificed part of himself. His mind.

00:07:25.230 --> 00:07:29.110
His soul. All of these he sacrificed to write.

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:31.650
That's who Ryunosuke Akutagawa was!

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:39.980
You said you liked his works,

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:42.320
but you didn't realize at all!

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:43.650
Realize what?

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:51.820
That the process of creating them
is what killed him!

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:55.360
He suffered to write.

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:57.440
He worried as he wrote.

00:07:57.440 --> 00:07:59.820
And even as he wrote, he sobbed.

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:03.110
And I saw it all!

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:43.440
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> ...

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:50.070
I changed this story of pain.

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:56.820
Look at his expression now that the pain
of writing has been taken from him.

00:08:56.820 --> 00:09:02.110
Without writing, he can be so happy.

00:09:02.110 --> 00:09:04.030
That smile...

00:09:04.030 --> 00:09:06.530
That's how a man should be.

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:10.650
He'll never kill himself now.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:14.780
This is Ryunosuke Akutagawa
in a world without literature.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:19.030
This is the happy world he belongs in.

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:36.070
What?

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:40.150
<i>Old Age</i> . <i>The Death of the Christian</i> .

00:09:40.150 --> 00:09:42.820
<i>Rashomon</i> . <i>Nose</i> .

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:44.360
<i>Tobacco and the Devil</i> .

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:45.570
<i>Luck</i> .

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:46.820
<i>The Spider's Thread</i> .

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:51.030
What are you doing?

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:53.650
<i>Portrait of Hell</i> !

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:58.320
What? What's going on?

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:02.190
<i>Jashumon</i> . <i>The Dance Party</i> . <i>The God of Aguni</i> .

00:10:02.190 --> 00:10:05.320
<i>In a Bamboo Grove</i> ! <i>Trolley</i> ! <i>Kappa</i> !

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:07.820
<i>Mirage</i> ! <i>Gears</i> !

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:13.150
All of them are carved into my heart.

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:14.570
Not just me!

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:20.940
They exist in the hearts of many,
sometimes even changing their lives!

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:24.980
None of them can be allowed to disappear.

00:10:24.980 --> 00:10:26.650
Stop!

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:28.150
Stop it!

00:10:38.230 --> 00:10:39.730
And it was so much fun, too...

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:45.360
What's wrong?

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:49.440
Nothing's wrong.

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:53.190
Nothing's wrong. But...

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:55.480
Somehow...

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:59.070
...it felt as if you were going to die.

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:02.030
I see.

00:11:03.730 --> 00:11:06.150
I'm sorry, Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> ...

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:09.690
I... I...

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:11.980
I wanted you to die!

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:33.960
Final Episode

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:44.030
What are you doing?

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:46.030
What are you thinking?

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:49.070
Do you know what you've done?

00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:53.570
You told Ryunosuke Akutagawa
that he needed to die!

00:11:56.900 --> 00:11:59.190
Why didn't you dodge?

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:01.730
I couldn't.

00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:04.360
Because behind me...

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:06.400
...is literature!

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:11.570
What good is literature if it makes
people suffer? Drives them to suicide?

00:12:11.570 --> 00:12:13.150
Enough.

00:12:13.150 --> 00:12:18.030
I just need to get rid of you
and then taint it again.

00:12:18.030 --> 00:12:23.610
I'm going to save my beloved friend's life...
no matter what it takes!

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:27.480
Shatter and disappear like the other authors!

00:12:30.190 --> 00:12:33.110
I won't disappear!

00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:42.570
Even if my soul shatters...

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:51.900
Even if my soul... shattered...

00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:56.280
...my feelings will not!

00:12:56.280 --> 00:12:57.530
This is...

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:10.980
My weapon?

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:14.360
So the laws were changed?

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:21.650
It's too late for that to matter!

00:13:43.980 --> 00:13:46.530
You're a mess.

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:47.690
Loser.

00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:49.360
Shiga!

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:50.650
It ain't just me.

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:02.360
We're back, Dazai!

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:25.860
Dazai. Let's go.

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:33.110
Let's go, everyone!

00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:38.730
I'm in a bad mood!

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:41.110
Don't blame me if you die!

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:45.230
Kikuchi- <i>san</i> , you need to calm down a bit.

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:46.940
It's fine.

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:49.940
I feel like kicking some butt too.

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:01.360
Dan!

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:03.150
What are you doing, Dazai?

00:15:03.150 --> 00:15:04.480
You look like a loser.

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:07.070
You don't know what I've been through!

00:15:07.070 --> 00:15:10.650
No, I can tell you've been through a lot!

00:15:13.280 --> 00:15:17.190
And I've got a special dish
to make you later as a reward!

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:24.280
Shiga.

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:27.150
Oh, Musha.

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:29.440
Huh?

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:31.480
It's been forever-- ow!

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:32.940
What was that for?

00:15:32.940 --> 00:15:35.400
Do you know how much I've worried?

00:15:37.320 --> 00:15:38.940
Sorry.

00:15:38.940 --> 00:15:43.440
I'll forgive you if you work
ten times as much as I do.

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:45.610
There you go again.

00:15:56.610 --> 00:15:57.940
I'm tired.

00:15:57.940 --> 00:16:00.280
Shimazaki! No slacking off.

00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:02.530
You work hard, Shusei.

00:16:02.530 --> 00:16:05.980
You're so boring. So for once...

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:08.280
Stop calling me boring!

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:15.070
They don't stop coming!

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:16.280
Don't worry.

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:18.400
I won't stop shooting!

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:19.230
What?

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:24.320
As long as you're here, I can fight forever!

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:35.230
I'm a bad shot, huh?

00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:36.940
As always.

00:16:36.940 --> 00:16:39.070
The boss is mine!

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:50.940
I've come to pay you back.

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:04.230
Not bad!

00:17:24.110 --> 00:17:25.280
You...

00:18:03.070 --> 00:18:05.530
Die!

00:18:29.570 --> 00:18:30.860
Finish it, Dazai!

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:32.190
Go for it!

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:30.190
Not yet...

00:19:31.280 --> 00:19:32.980
I'm still not...

00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:37.280
Dazai!

00:19:56.150 --> 00:19:57.440
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> !

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:07.400
Shiga- <i>san</i> .

00:20:07.400 --> 00:20:08.400
Right!

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:13.610
Let's settle this. Just you and I.

00:20:47.860 --> 00:20:51.780
Are you okay with this?

00:20:51.780 --> 00:20:52.900
Yes.

00:20:52.900 --> 00:20:54.730
I am.

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:57.730
You don't suffer?

00:20:57.730 --> 00:21:00.030
I suffer to the point of death.

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:03.900
But that's what an author is.

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:15.650
How beautiful...

00:21:17.190 --> 00:21:21.690
Thank you for living alongside me.

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:25.230
Thank you, my friend.

00:22:08.030 --> 00:22:11.110
It's bent a little.

00:22:11.110 --> 00:22:14.030
Are you making me do all the work?

00:22:14.030 --> 00:22:16.690
Where do I put this?

00:22:19.820 --> 00:22:21.030
Seriously.

00:22:21.030 --> 00:22:23.360
Oh, well, it all worked out.

00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:26.690
This is...

00:22:26.690 --> 00:22:28.570
Just like we heard.

00:22:30.320 --> 00:22:32.320
Special <i>ango</i> soup!

00:22:32.320 --> 00:22:35.110
Now with triple the taste of corruption!

00:22:36.610 --> 00:22:38.280
Eat up!

00:22:38.280 --> 00:22:40.610
'Cause there's lots more!

00:22:43.780 --> 00:22:46.400
You can't be exhausted already!

00:22:46.400 --> 00:22:49.400
We've got a lot of work to do
to get to our paradise!

00:22:51.150 --> 00:22:53.190
Fine.

00:22:53.190 --> 00:22:54.820
I'll play along!

00:22:54.820 --> 00:23:00.820
Jeez... they stop working when it gets peaceful.

00:23:00.820 --> 00:23:04.980
But the Taints aren't gone.

00:23:04.980 --> 00:23:12.530
As long as they exist and threaten literature,
the battle will continue.

00:23:12.530 --> 00:23:15.570
But no matter how fierce the foe,

00:23:15.570 --> 00:23:18.940
I won't let them destroy
the emotions of the authors.

00:23:18.940 --> 00:23:21.820
As long as the authors and Alchemist exist...

00:23:25.980 --> 00:23:27.480
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> !

00:23:28.940 --> 00:23:30.530
Trouble!

00:23:30.530 --> 00:23:32.190
Doubtless. Goodnight.

00:23:32.190 --> 00:23:34.530
No, there's no time to sleep!

00:23:34.530 --> 00:23:36.900
A Taint has appeared!

00:23:39.530 --> 00:23:40.690
Let's go!

00:23:48.110 --> 00:23:49.320
Sensei!

00:23:57.740 --> 00:24:00.940
Fin
